   "format": "mcq",
   "stem": {
      "text": "Let \\( g \\) be the function defined by \\( g(x) = \\int_{2}^{x} \\left(t(t - 3)(t - 8)\\right) \\, dt \\) for \\( 1 < x < 10 \\). Find the value of \\( x \\) at which \\( g \\) has a relative minimum."
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": 8
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "By the Fundamental Theorem of Calculus, \\( g'(x) = x(x - 3)(x - 8) \\) for \\( 1 < x < 10 \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Multiply",
            "x",
            [
               "Add",
               "x",
               -8
            ],
            [
               "Add",
               "x",
               -3
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Set \\( g'(x) = 0 \\) and factor: \\( x(x - 3)(x - 8) = 0 \\), so \\( x = 0, 3, 8 \\).",
         "mathjson": 8
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "Only \\( x = 3 \\) and \\( x = 8 \\) lie in \\( 1 < x < 10 \\); \\( x = 0 \\) is outside the interval on which \\( g \\) is defined, so it is not a critical point of \\( g \\).",
         "mathjson": 8
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "\\( g' \\) changes from negative to positive at \\( x = 8 \\) and from positive to negative at \\( x = 3 \\), so \\( g \\) has its relative minimum at \\( x = 8 \\).",
         "mathjson": 8
      }
   ],
